{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting","id":1470529,"title":"How do vampires maintain security while hunting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-15T08:28:45-08:00","id":1470529,"title":"How do vampires maintain security while hunting?","content":"It's something I thought about when playing Coteries of New York. Your mentor routinely hunts out in the open with just one ghoul. If someone wanted to assassinate her, it doesn't seem like it would have been particularly difficult. How do elder vampires protect themselves when out hunting? Do most of them keep an army of heavily armed ghouls around at all times when out seducing in clubs, breaking into the homes of sleepers, and mugging alleyway bums? For the supposedly &quot;social&quot; class of monsters, it sure does seem like much of their existence is highly impractical to do as anything but a loner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T09:13:33-08:00","id":1470532,"title":"","content":"I imagine most Elders have their food come to them. The risk it's that whatever net they use to do this, at least one link must connect to where they eat. But anyway taking advantage of that it's not as easy as waiting in the street, as such a place can be heavily defended. If an Elder hunts in a club, most likely it's her club.<br /> <br /> Exceptions could be vampires that *like* to hunt personaly and out there (Gangrel being the typical example). But these prob. are very good at the hunt, and at not becoming preys themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-15-2021, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T11:32:29-08:00","id":1470537,"title":"","content":"With the size of cities compared to vampire population, keeping a low profile while hunting isn't exceptionally hard. As long as you keep your enemies from learning your feeding habits, you shouldn't have that much of a problem. Even then this is one of the reasons to have feeding grounds strictly defined and enforced. An elder probably do not hunt over an entire borough, but will want to know who exactly, if anyone among the Damned, is even stepping there.<br /> <br /> That aside, power in all its forms is used to keep protection. You want people to know that messing with you isn't without consequence, whatever this consequence might be. This is one reason for the Camarilla to be real on its enforcement of the Traditions: laws that work bring safety, and the first priority of an elder isn't to kill opponents or even Thin Bloods, but to not die. The Sabbat keeps the Vaulderie and the Packs for similar reasons, without the protection of the law, always have at reach someone you can thrust enough to not kill you, and preferably kill anyone who tries.<br /> <br /> Bringing your food to you is the ultimate prize. It doesn't matter if one of your heavens is a VIP club or if your thugs kidnap beggars and bring them for you, safeguarding a place and have your victims coming is one of the safest options. Having the blood brought to you at a different place from where it was extracted is even safer, and most elders won't let taste stay in the way of safety on common nights. Any Tremere that knows rituals to keep blood fresh and tasty in a bottle is in for making a lot of money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T12:01:53-08:00","id":1470540,"title":"","content":"First, the grand strategy: Don't make enemies, or at least serious enemies. A petty rivalry might be fun, so long as both parties know the rules, but if someone doesn't know the rules? Axe em. Target ambitious bastards that make you worry, but do it secretly; if you succeed, they're dead or they learn their lesson, if you fail, you shouldn't be a suspect. You can do a lot by building good relationships with everyone, though of course sometimes getting too friendly with Vampire A might upset Vampire B. <br /> <br /> A stable government that keeps some semblance of law and order will help you live longer. Your politics should always favour stability. <br /> <br /> Second, the Tactics. <br /> <br /> There's a hundred ways to hunt and each clan is generally going to approach feeding differently. The Tremere and Ventrue control their environments. The Nosferatu and Malkavians don't let people know they were ever there. The Brujah and Toreador are really the interesting ones. The Toreador need to be selective and they've got the tools to be selective, Auspex helps you find problems, celerity helps you avoid problems, and Presence helps deter problems: they benefit from large crowds that prevent violence helps.. The Brujah are... well, if you can kill the Brujah in the first round, GG, if you fail to kill the Brujah in the first round, GG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T21:35:46-08:00","id":1472936,"title":"","content":"When you get down to it, if somebody puts it in their head and takes the time for it, most vampires can be assassinated, hunt or no hunt. A daytime raid with enough determination behind it can end the vast majority of vampires. The balance of power within a city is something like mutually assured destruction: an outsider may not know where the havens of everybody are, but the longtime residents of cities are intimately familiar with where they each lair. Few vampires are protected sufficiently from this: a major Tremere chantry might survive if warded enough, and some havens may be obscured by elder levels of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> While you cannot really prevent an assassination attempt on you from succeeding, you can definitely deter an easy attempt from having a chance. If it would take a dozen trained ghouls to take you down in the daytime, for example, that's too big an operation and would cause serious enough ripples to bring an Archon to the city. But if two ghouls could take you down, everybody is going to be tempted if they see any gain in it. So a few booby traps and a few armed ghouls in each haven typically keeps the peace.<br /> <br /> A similar logic operates in the case of hunting. Celerity, Obfuscate, Protean, Vicissitude, Serpentis, Chimerstry, and Fortitude are all great for getting away from an ambush; Auspex helps you see it coming. If you're weak enough to get gibbed by a few armed ghouls or neonates, people will be tempted to inconvenience you during feeding. If everybody knows you have a fighting chance or could somehow get away, they would have to put together experienced Kindred to whack you, and the Prince will notice. If you sufficiently annoy somebody with connections, they can contract an Assamite onto you and you have practically no chance; but that's why everybody's polite to each other's faces in Elysium, always.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, there's a tradeoff between convenience and safety. You could have your ghouls bring you meals like a lot of paranoid elders do, but then you grow out of touch with the world and with your Humanity. It's also horrible: imagine the part of the lockdown where you sat at home all day and had delivery, but have it span a few centuries. Also note that in vampiric power, charisma and courage count for a lot. If you're too chicken to step out of your haven and stretch your legs, other vampires won't see you as a leader, and others will come to dominate city affairs. Only elders with powers like Auspex 6, Dominate 8 etc. can really afford to direct events from a distance (Tzimisce, Lasombra. Ventrue elders).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13688-sultanabdal","name":"Sultanabdal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13688_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T07:09:13-08:00","id":1472962,"title":"","content":"Many aspects of V:tM falls apart when you focus in on logistics or logic. Between the ability to have a live in Herd, online banking, the Internet, and video conferences.... there really isn't a reason for a vampire to leave their havens, which in today's world can easily be a converted decommissioned nuclear missile silo or similar military grade secure installation.<br /> <br /> The notion of vampire society is more of a game mechanic on par with having a party meeting in a tavern or inn. It helps create role play situations rather than give an accurate simulation of creatures with the abilities and proclivities we know and love.<br /> <br /> As for the idea of hunting, in truth it should really be a feeding method used by traveling vampires rather than established locals. Any Clan/Bloodline with Animalism, Dominate, or Presence should really have a Herd background. Clans with Obfuscate would be the main ones to &quot;hunt&quot; in the modern era. But once again if we are talking about Elders, they would travel with a herd in tow rather than hunting.<br /> <br /> At the same time, while it is logical to say that assassinating a target while they are hunting, the reality of it is that you probably won't know when a target will go hunting, and more importantly where they will hunt. At best you can follow a target to their hunting grounds and hopefully be able to sneak up on them, but you won't be able to set up a proper ambush. Any vampire worth their fangs will have four or five hunting areas and switch between them at random, usually with a travel route that allows them to spot any uninvited guests.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T10:25:28-08:00","id":1472978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1472962#post1472962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many aspects of V:tM falls apart when you focus in on logistics or logic. Between the ability to have a live in Herd, online banking, the Internet, and video conferences.... there really isn't a reason for a vampire to leave their havens, which in today's world can easily be a converted decommissioned nuclear missile silo or similar military grade secure installation.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I go to the mall I often see a blood donation truck set up in the parking lot that I'm sure makes rounds at other locations as well. If I was a vampire I'd get in on that action with a ghoul dropping off bags to my home after a days work. I do think the missile silo is still out of the price range of most all vampires to be honest, but electronic banking makes things easier. You probably do still need humans to do the stuff for you so they age and function during the day, trading them out for new ones in our ever shrinking world of endless data collection. Facial recognition software is the true new bane coming to the immortal not wanting to be found out as more and more cameras are plugged into the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T11:12:23-08:00","id":1472983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1472978#post1472978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I go to the mall I often see a blood donation truck set up in the parking lot that I'm sure makes rounds at other locations as well. If I was a vampire I'd get in on that action with a ghoul dropping off bags to my home after a days work.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blood Drive/Blood Bank routine is a functional option, except it comes with a few potential negatives. Depending on edition, spiking the blood bags with vampire blood to try to cause a blood bond wasn't uncommon. Also enemies can follow the blood mobile back to your haven or they can lay a trap at the blood bank.<br /> <br /> In one game I played in, the coterie got shipments of blood bags delivered to their haven, the only problem was the enemies found out and put in some C4 and a tripwire connected to the lid at the bottom of the ice chest. That coterie didn't survive for long with their lackluster security practices.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1472978#post1472978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think the missile silo is still out of the price range of most all vampires to be honest, but electronic banking makes things easier. You probably do still need humans to do the stuff for you so they age and function during the day, trading them out for new ones in our ever shrinking world of endless data collection. Facial recognition software is the true new bane coming to the immortal not wanting to be found out as more and more cameras are plugged into the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Current decommissioned silo prices are about $500,000 to buy the land and silo. Even if you spent another $250,000 on retrofitting it to your exact needs, it is still cheaper than buying a one million dollar home or mini-mansion. Or as big city Californians call them &quot;a three bedroom, two bath, fixer upper&quot;. All joking aside, that means the missile silo haven is around Resources 4 for a single vampire or far more viable for a coterie that pools their Resource backgrounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-22T10:46:32-08:00","id":1473035,"title":"","content":"Most vampires are indeed reclusive in this way, espcially elders; once they establish a turf and a herd and get the ok from the Prince to stay, they tend to hunker down. PCs are by definition a rare exception; most vampires don't go questing around.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite clans to play is the Ravnos, because their clan weakness prevents them from ossifying in this way. Whatever their criminal weakness is, theft, assault etc., they have to go out there and indulge in them, and eventually bring down heat on themselves. Since a Ravnos is a one-man crimewave, travel is necessary to spread this out and not be so noticeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13688-sultanabdal","name":"Sultanabdal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13688_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T00:27:44-08:00","id":1473063,"title":"","content":"This is one of the reasons why creating Elder NPCs is often done so poorly. Most STs and writers concentrate on the Disciplines that an Elder possesses rather than the vast array of high level backgrounds they should have.<br /> <br /> e.g. I think that any serious Elder would be expected to have most of the following:<br /> <br /> Resources 4+<br /> Allies 2+<br /> Contacts 4+<br /> Domain 5+, probably more like 10-15<br /> Herd 4+<br /> Influence 3+<br /> Retainers 2+<br /> Status 3+","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T06:12:32-08:00","id":1473069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473063#post1473063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the reasons why creating Elder NPCs is often done so poorly. Most STs and writers concentrate on the Disciplines that an Elder possesses rather than the vast array of high level backgrounds they should have.<br /> <br /> e.g. I think that any serious Elder would be expected to have most of the following:<br /> <br /> Resources 4+<br /> Allies 2+<br /> Contacts 4+<br /> Domain 5+, probably more like 10-15<br /> Herd 4+<br /> Influence 3+<br /> Retainers 2+<br /> Status 3+</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that many elders are in general, poorly thought out.<br /> <br /> As for the Background point spread, I think it would look more like this.<br /> <br /> Allies: 3+<br /> Alternate Identity: 3<br /> Contacts: 5<br /> Domain: 0<br /> Fame: 0<br /> Herd: 2<br /> Influence: 2+<br /> Resources: 5<br /> Retainers: 3+<br /> Status: 3+<br /> <br /> Unless you are burning a lot of bp every night, anything larger than a level 2 Herd doesn't grant a benefit. Likewise, if you have a Herd at home, you have no use for Domain, not to mention since an elder would be less publicly active they wouldn't want to constantly be defending hunting territory from youngsters. <br /> <br /> Also I see elders being a bit more detached from the every day mortal concerns of a given area, hence the lower Influence score and lack of Fame. The elder could probably crush any political party, public official, or local influencer, but that is more a side affect of having a few million in cash to throw at a problem rather than being deeply connected.<br /> <br /> The Alternate Identity is more just a function that an Elder knows if they do something in their own name, everyone will take notice. Having a side identity allows for greater security and less attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T11:07:53-08:00","id":1473088,"title":"","content":"I disagree that there's no reason to have Domain or a Herd greater than 2. There's a very good reason to have both: Redundancy.<br /> <br /> No matter how secure a vampire appears, setbacks can snowball into catastrophic problems. You don't want to be the Elder who relies on a pool of vessels, only for half of them to be taken out of commission, beyond the vampire's reach, tainted by disease, or actively targeted.<br /> <br /> A vampire keeps more Herd so they can soak losses without significant disruption of their regular feeding. That same vampire seeks to retain control of a Domain, so they always have the option of doing an old fashioned hunt in territory they control. Just having that option is worth its weight in gold.<br /> <br /> Especially if, despite the Elder's best efforts, they end up making enemies that are willing to escalate matters. We can talk all day about the best defense against being targeted is to not make enemies in the first place. Reality is rarely so accommodating, and the Jyhad even less so.<br /> <br /> We must also remember that Elders, like all people, are not perfectly rational beings that only ever make the most efficient decisions. A vampire will seek to acquire more Herd, because the caveman part of the brain (to whatever degree that remains in the dead corpus that they call a body) still hews to that most simple adage: more food = better.<br /> <br /> By that same token, no matter the level of sophistication at play in the Elder's mind, the Beast is gratified by having territory it can call its own. Seeking to acquire and expand Domain is, often, felt to be a good unto itself. The ability to say &quot;this place is MINE, stay out!&quot; is all the reason an Elder needs to do so. And when a city has been carved up between Kindred power players, the only way to get more Domain is to shave it off a rival.<br /> <br /> Hence the Jyhad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T11:59:02-08:00","id":1473092,"title":"","content":"As far as backgrounds go, I find some of them are better left to retainers. A couple strong ghouls can take care of a lot of the mortal things kind of beneath a centuries old vampire. I would think most elders have nurtured a couple strong ghouls and created a couple Childer to delegate to.<br /> <br /> I really like the alternate rules for Domain in DAV20 Companion, where it gets scores for Area, Defense, Prosperity, and Secret Ways. They actually had an interesting take on other backgrounds as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T12:55:59-08:00","id":1473100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473088#post1473088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree that there's no reason to have Domain or a Herd greater than 2. There's a very good reason to have both: Redundancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>While redundancy is a good strategy, the scope of it is what I am disagreeing with.<br /> <br /> Why have a larger herd, which must be maintained by the way, when you can own hospitals and blood banks. Alternatively, you don't have to own those places, you can just have a really high-grade medical coverage plan that lets you get &quot;transfusions&quot; anywhere in the country. Unless you are running a compound where the Herd never leave, each additional herd member is a potential security hazard. Just having more of them doesn't solve a problem or prevent one, it just adds to security hassles.<br /> <br /> Even if you do go the hole private herd in my basement route, have you considered the logistics of housing, feeding, and upkeep on that many people? The average american home only has about 3 days supplies in it. Without a lot of planning and investment there is no way to survive a siege with a large herd for any meaningful length of time.<br /> <br /> Domain is the same scenario, why claim a domain that you have to defend. That basically is putting up a huge neon sign saying &quot;find this elder here&quot;. Since most Elders tend to have lower Generations than most of the locals, that is just endless conflict waiting to happen for nothing more than bragging rights to an eating area. Of course just become you are an Elder and claim Domain, it doesn't mean a younger upstart Prince won't just declare immanent domain and seize it or declare it a public hunting area.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it is just my way of thinking, but Elders should never be &quot;the Lost Boys&quot; but with bigger bank accounts and older clothing fashion. That focus on street level things is left behind after a certain age bracket. Does this mean that most game storylines actually don't work with Elders, unfortunately yes. There are still plenty of cool games to be played with them, but they won't interact in the same way with the world as younger vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T21:15:43-08:00","id":1473138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473100#post1473100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While redundancy is a good strategy, the scope of it is what I am disagreeing with.<br /> <br /> Why have a larger herd, which must be maintained by the way, when you can own hospitals and blood banks. Alternatively, you don't have to own those places, you can just have a really high-grade medical coverage plan that lets you get &quot;transfusions&quot; anywhere in the country. Unless you are running a compound where the Herd never leave, each additional herd member is a potential security hazard. Just having more of them doesn't solve a problem or prevent one, it just adds to security hassles.<br /> <br /> Even if you do go the hole private herd in my basement route, have you considered the logistics of housing, feeding, and upkeep on that many people? The average american home only has about 3 days supplies in it. Without a lot of planning and investment there is no way to survive a siege with a large herd for any meaningful length of time.<br /> <br /> Domain is the same scenario, why claim a domain that you have to defend. That basically is putting up a huge neon sign saying &quot;find this elder here&quot;. Since most Elders tend to have lower Generations than most of the locals, that is just endless conflict waiting to happen for nothing more than bragging rights to an eating area. Of course just become you are an Elder and claim Domain, it doesn't mean a younger upstart Prince won't just declare immanent domain and seize it or declare it a public hunting area.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it is just my way of thinking, but Elders should never be &quot;the Lost Boys&quot; but with bigger bank accounts and older clothing fashion. That focus on street level things is left behind after a certain age bracket. Does this mean that most game storylines actually don't work with Elders, unfortunately yes. There are still plenty of cool games to be played with them, but they won't interact in the same way with the world as younger vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're taking a lot of things too literally.<br /> <br /> A Herd is just a group of people that provide you with blood in a way that doesn't require any danger on your part or &quot;hunting.&quot;<br /> <br /> A typical herd for, say, a smexy vampire might be a Black Book or Cell Phone contacts list of women (or men) ready to &quot;have sex&quot; with you at any time you call them. They might also be all the employees at your office building that know that getting called to the office for a meeting results in being sick for days afterward (presumably from stress). It might also be the fact you run a hotel that you have keys to so you can feed on sleeping residents with impunity.<br /> <br /> Generally, at least how V5 runs it, I also think the vast majority of vampires have Domain if they're playing by the rules. Just because it makes it much easier for you to know where and what you can feed on without worrying about someone else getting it. A fairly easy adventure I run for newbie V:TM gamers is &quot;The Poacher.&quot; Which is the PCs have been given a domain that's really small but useful, say a block of buildings, and a couple of dead humans have shown up there.<br /> <br /> Under law vampire, you have the right to pursue this asshole who have been feeding on &quot;your&quot; humans.<br /> <br /> Having domain lets you protect some mortals from being killed.<br /> <br /> And Blood Banks and Hospitals are probably very sought after domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T03:54:35-08:00","id":1473156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473100#post1473100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While redundancy is a good strategy, the scope of it is what I am disagreeing with.<br /> <br /> Why have a larger herd, which must be maintained by the way, when you can own hospitals and blood banks.</div> </div> </div> </div>As CTPhipps said, having control over a hospital or blood bank IS having dots Herd and/or Domain. If I were the Storyteller in charge, that is absolutely how I would rule it.<br /> <br /> It is consistent with the intent behind those backgrounds: consistent sources of blood the vampire doesn't have to work for, and a location under the vampire's control that can be legally denied to other vampires, respectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless you are running a compound where the Herd never leave, each additional herd member is a potential security hazard. Just having more of them doesn't solve a problem or prevent one, it just adds to security hassles.<br /> <br /> Even if you do go the hole private herd in my basement route, have you considered the logistics of housing, feeding, and upkeep on that many people? The average american home only has about 3 days supplies in it. Without a lot of planning and investment there is no way to survive a siege with a large herd for any meaningful length of time. </div> </div> </div>That's not actually a strike against the concept, though. The game is not obligated to make Herd a free background with no upkeep or downsides. Having one's Herd be vulnerable to being disrupted is just the cost of doing business in the vampire world.<br /> <br /> Again, that's the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> Moreover, my suggestion was in response to the assumption that Herd 2 was alright, but any more was not worth it. Well, ANY amount of Herd is going to vulnerable to something. Redundancy is the way to deal with that.<br /> <br /> If anything, the fact that Herd is a security issue is all the more reason to expand and diversify. If any given vessel or source of blood (like a blood bank) can be targeted, having more of them insulates the vampire from attacks against it.<br /> <br /> It is not unreasonable for an Elder to think as you do, and say that having more Herd is more trouble than it's worth. That's a perfectly valid motivation for some Elders. But it's also perfectly valid for an Elder to think as I do, by diversifying &quot;revenue&quot; sources. On the assumption that it's impossible to protect everything, all the time, so it's easier to just cast a wider net.<br /> <br /> Is this necessarily the smartest thing? Maybe, maybe not. But, as I said in my previous post, vampires are not perfectly rational actors. They are &quot;allowed&quot; to make bad decisions.<br /> <br /> Especially if they creates conflict in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Domain is the same scenario, why claim a domain that you have to defend. That basically is putting up a huge neon sign saying &quot;find this elder here&quot;. Since most Elders tend to have lower Generations than most of the locals, that is just endless conflict waiting to happen for nothing more than bragging rights to an eating area. </div> </div> </div>Again, that's the Jyhad for you. Endless conflict is sort of the name of the game.<br /> <br /> Moreover, while I stated in the previous post that Elders need no other reason to hold Domain other than the animalistic urge to have it - and I stand by this - there are plenty of practical reasons to hold Domain.<ul><li>Having a hunting ground that other vampires aren't legally allowed to enter. In turn, giving you the right to murder any vampire trespassing in that Domain.</li> <li>Having a part of the community or essential infrastructure that another vampire cannot legally interfere with. If your Domain is the police, no one else is allowed to manipulate the police without your permission.</li> <li>Speaking of permission, Domain is not merely valuable for its ability to be denied to other vampires, but because access can be offered at the Domain holder's discretion. Whether as hunting ground or in its own right, access to the Domain is a bargaining chip the vampire can leverage to their own advantage. Elders carving up a city between them isn't just for their own edification, it's to allow them to strong-arm younger licks into doing what the Elders want or risk starvation.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course just become you are an Elder and claim Domain, it doesn't mean a younger upstart Prince won't just declare immanent domain and seize it or declare it a public hunting area. </div> </div> </div>That depends on how powerful the Prince is. Remember, the power structures of Kindred politics are built on a Kindred's ability to enforce their will. An upstart Prince can declare eminent domain over anything they please. What matters is whether they're strong enough to make that claim stick.<br /> <br /> In some cities, Princes are strong enough that other vampires must acquiesce to their demands. In other cities, it's the other way around. Lodin, the archetypal Prince in VtM, was in reality subordinate to the Primogen who actually controlled Chicago.<br /> <br /> If a Prince is strong enough to claim an Elder's Domain by fiat, they better be able to make that claim stick. Otherwise, they're looking at a reprisal that may be bloody. Especially if the Elders, collectively, decide that the upstart Prince's ability to take one Elder's Domain means they might do it to all of them, so it's in their collective best interest to gang up on him. Eliminate the upstart, before they can consolidate power.<br /> <br /> This is by no means guaranteed. The Jyhad is complicated, and depends greatly on the local balance of power and the interests of the Kindred involved. But this is <b>A</b> way the situation can go. Kindred politics has a lot of give and take. A lot of jockeying for position. Vampires only gain resources by taking them, often from other, more established licks. Power plays are made. Sometimes, these plays don't work. Often, there is retribution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps it is just my way of thinking, but Elders should never be &quot;the Lost Boys&quot; but with bigger bank accounts and older clothing fashion. That focus on street level things is left behind after a certain age bracket. Does this mean that most game storylines actually don't work with Elders, unfortunately yes. There are still plenty of cool games to be played with them, but they won't interact in the same way with the world as younger vampires. </div> </div> </div>I would argue that vampires, being creatures of Stasis, leave behind old ways less readily than one would imagine. Moreover, Elder vampires are very much like the mafia. A veneer of respectability, stretched over a truth of violence, exploitation, and power politics. Indeed, while an Elder would rankle at being compared to gangs scrambling over city streets as &quot;turf&quot;, that's more or less exactly what they are.<br /> <br /> If anything, playing into that is Vampire: The Masquerade at its most thematically consistent. For all the posturing of old vampires, they are little better than their younger rivals. They are violent predators that seek to claim stretches of territory, even if it means protecting it with brutal violence. It doesn't matter that the Elder will send minions to break legs for them. Their Domains are still, ultimately, violently enforced. Even if they spend most of their unlives in courts or art galleries, or building stock portfolios, they will still have an upstart murdered for touching their stuff.<br /> <br /> That's not a contradiction in terms. That's pathos. That's Punk.<br /> <br /> We need to ask ourselves not why the classic VtM dynamic doesn't work. We need to ask ourselves how Elders need to think in order to MAKE it work. The world-building of VtM exists to serve the needs of the roleplaying game, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Luckily, we don't need to stretch to make street level games involving Elders work. Elders are flawed individuals, whose actions are not always perfectly rational. They're just older, more powerful, more entrenched. More <i>entitled</i>. They may even delude themselves into thinking they're better than the Neonates scrambling for sustenance in the slums. But they're just another parasite.<br /> <br /> Making them all completely absent from the night-to-night operations of vampire unlife is not only unlikely - no Elder can maintain their operations without having a power base, especially when Diablerie is a factor - it's also contrary to the needs of the game. Why even have them in the setting if they aren't going to be a source of risk or opportunity for vampire PCs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 01-24-2022, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T04:11:53-08:00","id":1473159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473138#post1473138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're taking a lot of things too literally.<br /> <br /> A Herd is just a group of people that provide you with blood in a way that doesn't require any danger on your part or &quot;hunting.&quot;<br /> <br /> A typical herd for, say, a smexy vampire might be a Black Book or Cell Phone contacts list of women (or men) ready to &quot;have sex&quot; with you at any time you call them. They might also be all the employees at your office building that know that getting called to the office for a meeting results in being sick for days afterward (presumably from stress). It might also be the fact you run a hotel that you have keys to so you can feed on sleeping residents with impunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly I detest V5 so I tend to use V20 as the default so it is entirely possible there is some cross edition differences. With that being said Herd is a group that you bring together or build, not randoms in an area that are easy to feed from, which ironically enough would be covered by Domain. Your examples of feeding off of hotel residents or office workers is technically Domain, not Herd.<br /> <br /> The exact description is:<br /> &quot;You have built a group of mortals from whom you can feed without fear. A herd may take many forms, from circles of kinky clubgoers to actual cults built around you as a god-figure.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473138#post1473138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, at least how V5 runs it, I also think the vast majority of vampires have Domain if they're playing by the rules. Just because it makes it much easier for you to know where and what you can feed on without worrying about someone else getting it. A fairly easy adventure I run for newbie V:TM gamers is &quot;The Poacher.&quot; Which is the PCs have been given a domain that's really small but useful, say a block of buildings, and a couple of dead humans have shown up there.<br /> <br /> Under law vampire, you have the right to pursue this asshole who have been feeding on &quot;your&quot; humans.<br /> <br /> Having domain lets you protect some mortals from being killed.<br /> <br /> And Blood Banks and Hospitals are probably very sought after domains.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you notice in my previous posts, I am generally talking about Elders, not vampires of all age groups. Yes a Domain is great for story hooks for younger vampires, but ultimately an Elder doesn't gain enough benefits from having Domain compared to the security hassles involved in keeping it.<br /> <br /> Also I think we are coming at the story points from opposite ends of the Background spectrum. Lets break it down a bit to show the differences.<br /> <br /> Blood Bank/Hospital when accessed by the Resources background means that you own it, the same way you own your Haven or vehicle. Thus you can access the blood packs either completely legally or with only minor paperwork manipulation. As long as you own it, there isn't much in the way of hostile take overs or board membership changes that can threaten your access to what you need. Also it is worth noting that ownership in this case also means you have access to things beyond just the blood.<br /> <br /> Blood Bank/Hospital when accessed by the Domain background means that someone else owns and operates the institution and you just feed there. If you are breaking in after hours then you have to contend with security, if you are just trying to get blood via falsified paperwork then you have to hope the office drones aren't paying close attention.<br /> <br /> Blood Banks/Hospital when accessed by the Contact background is where you get the archetypal nurse or doctor selling blood packs under the table. Once again the location is owned by a third party.<br /> <br /> In short the Backgrounds system is based in abstraction rather than simulation, this is great for book keeping, but troublesome for figuring out what applies to it. Resources is a good example of how poorly it is abstracted, Resources 5 as a stat can describe a mortal with a few million in property ownership and less than 500k in the bank, it can describe people like Elon Musk, Jeff Bezos, or Bill Gates who are in the Multi-Billionaire category, or it can describe the obscenely rich kindred that the fluff always seems to reference as being many times richer than the richest mortals on earth so multi-trillionaire then?<br /> <br /> I wonder if certain things like Blood Banks/Hospitals should require a combination of backgrounds to get. Like you must have Resources, Domain, and Contacts to be able to lay claim to such a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T04:28:58-08:00","id":1473160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473156#post1473156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need to ask ourselves not why the classic VtM dynamic doesn't work. We need to ask ourselves how Elders need to think in order to MAKE it work. The world-building of VtM exists to serve the needs of the roleplaying game, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fundamentally disagree with this way of thinking because it hinges on breaking immersion, making bad characters, and poorly thought out plot lines to cover bad storytelling and world building.<br /> <br /> Your approach results in describing an Elder as a badass who has survived centuries or millennia of constant strife. They have more wealth than whole countries, private armies at their beck and call, and countless havens or safe houses across the nation or perhaps the world. But to fit the storyline that character then acts like a high school bully or clique member who is entirely focused on social interactions with lesser kindred. This is essentially like using MCU Thanos as the big bad, but then having him act like bugs bunny or daffy duck because otherwise the &quot;storylne&quot; wouldn't work or the party would get TPKed.<br /> <br /> The truth of the matter is that if you profile the Elder correctly, such a character probably wouldn't show up in your story the way you want to use them.<br /> <br /> A well built world with believable characters will always be fun to interact with. A storyline which breaks the world or the characters to suit the narrative of the moment... is less fun to play in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T05:28:32-08:00","id":1473161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473160#post1473160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I fundamentally disagree with this way of thinking because it hinges on breaking immersion, making bad characters, and poorly thought out plot lines to cover bad storytelling and world building.<br /> <br /> Your approach results in describing an Elder as a badass who has survived centuries or millennia of constant strife. They have more wealth than whole countries, private armies at their beck and call, and countless havens or safe houses across the nation or perhaps the world. But to fit the storyline that character then acts like a high school bully or clique member who is entirely focused on social interactions with lesser kindred. This is essentially like using MCU Thanos as the big bad, but then having him act like bugs bunny or daffy duck because otherwise the &quot;storylne&quot; wouldn't work or the party would get TPKed.<br /> <br /> The truth of the matter is that if you profile the Elder correctly, such a character probably wouldn't show up in your story the way you want to use them.<br /> <br /> A well built world with believable characters will always be fun to interact with. A storyline which breaks the world or the characters to suit the narrative of the moment... is less fun to play in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on what exactly you think an Elder IS.<br /> <br /> Karsh is like Thanos: an invincible personal badass who will wade into things with a battle axe himself.<br /> <br /> MOST Elders are like La Croix or Annabelle.<br /> <br /> They are social butterflies who have survived centuries by NOT getting into fights. For Toreador and Ventrue, their power depends on interacting with other Kindred and in fact their entire psychology is defined by gaining status from their fellow Kindred.<br /> <br /> A Ventrue is nothing alone.<br /> <br /> He needs the validation of lording over other beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T08:19:04-08:00","id":1473168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473160#post1473160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your approach results in describing an Elder as a badass who has survived centuries or millennia of constant strife. They have more wealth than whole countries, private armies at their beck and call, and countless havens or safe houses across the nation or perhaps the world. But to fit the storyline that character then acts like a high school bully or clique member who is entirely focused on social interactions with lesser kindred. This is essentially like using MCU Thanos as the big bad, but then having him act like bugs bunny or daffy duck because otherwise the &quot;storylne&quot; wouldn't work or the party would get TPKed.<br /> <br /> The truth of the matter is that if you profile the Elder correctly, such a character probably wouldn't show up in your story the way you want to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll say again the day to day Policing the Domain is something best done by Childer or underlings. If an elder rules a large section of a city, he's not actually going to be walking the streets, and will probably only get personally involved if things get out of hand. Delegation is a cornerstone of VTM as well.<br /> <br /> I enjoy your view and the view of others that oppose yours, but I think trying to give a hard definition to what an elder is is the problem here. You cannot make a minimum background dot list for elders because they are all unique unto themselves and like people their motivations, goals, and interests, as well as their tactics will vary. I think Retainers to handle mortal things, Childer to help enforce vampire things. Maybe an elder wants none of that, and simply drifts through time on his own finding subordinates lacking or uninteresting, uninterested in territory, or social interaction with his pears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T09:20:32-08:00","id":1473171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473168#post1473168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot make a minimum background dot list for elders because they are all unique unto themselves and like people their motivations, goals, and interests, as well as their tactics will vary. I think Retainers to handle mortal things, Childer to help enforce vampire things. Maybe an elder wants none of that, and simply drifts through time on his own finding subordinates lacking or uninteresting, uninterested in territory, or social interaction with his pears.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we are having a few different conversations here.<br /> <br /> An Elder is by definition just a vampire who has survived a long time. Now this can be accomplished by excessive amounts of topor which results in a vampire who has the age, but none of the experience of having existed for so long. This is simple enough to understand, but being an active Elder, there is the implication that the vampire has matured psychologically, gained patience, learned how not to overextend themselves, etc.<br /> <br /> In the Kindred of the East game line they had a term for younger vampires called a &quot;Running Monkey&quot; which described a Kuei-jin that was under one century old. They were expected to revel in their power, settle scores, and tidy up business from their mortal days. But after that century was up, it was essentially considered an embarrassment to act like that. As ritualized and organized as V:tM society is, the fluff never really addressed the notion of maturity as a social construct other than regarding paths of enlightenment. Though to be honest this could simply be a side of affect to V:tM being earlier in the game development cycle than KotE was.<br /> <br /> Getting back to defining an Elder, assuming they didn't snooze their way into the age bracket, that means that they would have had to survive that amount of time being active and interacting with the rest of the setting. I think we can all agree with that as a baseline, but where things break down is the ramifications of that statement and how some people hand wave it away.<br /> <br /> First off the vampire regardless of Path of Enlightenment will have demonstrated the psychological endurance for existing in the WoD for centuries or millennia. They are not going to have an existential crisis this late in the game, if they had a weakness to that they would either died/been killed off/resolved it within the first century or so of unlife.<br /> <br /> Second if a vampire Elder has a particular preference for how to do things, ie being a warrior, businessman, influencer, etc., then they will have the stats to support that in a meta kind of way. A vampire won't exist long enough to become an elder if they want to live as a warrior but then never learn combat disciplines or boost the related ability stats.<br /> <br /> Thirdly after having existed for so long, after a certain point the rewards of certain things just don't matter to you. As a child in kindergarten, we can easily be motivated by a gold star sticker, as a teenager we want validation from our peers, as adults.... well unless it has a paycheck, we don't care. There are certain aspects of vampiric existence that function the same way. Trying to have an Elder involved with certain storylines is really like suggesting that you can pay an adult in gold star stickers. Admittedly Malkavians throw that arguement out the window...<br /> <br /> In the end by the unforgiving nature of the WoD setting, an Elder has to be more of a Dark Souls player using banana controllers to do a speed run than a casual gamer playing a match three game on their break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T09:44:45-08:00","id":1473172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473168#post1473168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll say again the day to day Policing the Domain is something best done by Childer or underlings. If an elder rules a large section of a city, he's not actually going to be walking the streets, and will probably only get personally involved if things get out of hand. Delegation is a cornerstone of VTM as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another aspect that I often have issues with because of the rule of cool having a head on collision with RAW/fluff.<br /> <br /> Delegation only works if there are others to delegate to, ie more vampires. This becomes quite problematic when you remember that theoretically there are population limitations for vampires that are externally enforced. The local prince controls the rights of siring new childer, the clan hierarchy has rules about new embraces, or just the fact that too many vampires attract hunters or shifters.<br /> <br /> Many of our largest modern cities don't have enough human population to validate a vampire social club let alone a full vampiric society. In other words at the 1/100,000 ratio you are looking at less than 10 vampires per major population center. Now don't get me wrong, if you want to home brew the ratios or do a game where an upstart is just mass embracing like crazy in an attempt to destroy the masquerade, go for it. But in truth that isn't the setting. The setting is that while vampire could mass produce, then don't because they are careful or are culled for the good of all.<br /> <br /> So if vampires are rare enough that a single coterie accounts for practically all the vampires in a given city, then there really isn't much to defend against or fight over. Essentially the background of Domain breaks down because of low population numbers and only works if it is assumed that you have nightly visitations by roving gangs of vampire bikers from out of town.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to delegate to ghouls or just regular mortal minions, that makes far more sense. But ghouls and mortal minions don't really try to fight over things like Domain. Perhaps in addition to the 1/100,000 vampire to mortals ratio, White Wolf should add something about a Vampire to Ghouls ratio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T09:46:52-08:00","id":1473173,"title":"","content":"We may be talking about different things. I suppose my only point is we are never universal so you can't really say how every elder will feel, act, or spend his resources. I agree with priorities changing as we get older, but some work for love of whatever, never caring about the paycheck. I look at older (65+) people, some want to sit in front of the tv all day, some want to stay active outdoors, some still go to bars or restaurants to socialize most nights, some want to spend their days with family, some hang out with younger generations to stay young themselves.<br /> <br /> I just don't think every elder will take the same path, so I don't see a list of minimum backgrounds for all elders as anything other than a suggestion, not some hard and fast rule. Elders get more background dots, but they will spend them quite differently.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm saying I don't think any background is a requirement for survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 01-24-2022, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T11:23:45-08:00","id":1473181,"title":"","content":"My general take on ALL the various things here in this thread:<br /> <br /> <b>A shit ton of random V:TM thoughts about Domain</b><br /> <br /> 1. Generally, Elders are different from Methusalehs. An Elder tends to be someone who will probably avoid combat but does have a lot of exceptional powers. A Methuselah is effectively invincible from most vampires' standings.<br /> <br /> 2. Elders don't deal with mortals save as slaves so Elders CREATED the whole Elysium system so they can interact with vampires. The Toreador especially but all vampires really have their equivalents because vampires who aren't wights are social creatures.<br /> <br /> 3. Elders like having Domain because Domain is basically something that makes vampiredom easier and Elders are set in their ways. Every vampire wants to have an established hunting ground with no competition unless they're Gangrel or Ravnos.<br /> <br /> 4. Vampires will always pick &quot;from the tap&quot; over blood bags because blood bags are cold and nasty but will slake the Hunger if you're comically busy.<br /> <br /> 5. Herds can represent blood banks and hospitals too as well as Domain but generally represent mortals you have easy access to that won't put up a fight.<br /> <br /> 6. Not all vampires keep herds, not even all Elders, but it certainly is CONVEINANT. Like having wireless internet connection vs. going to a public wifi route.<br /> <br /> 7. Generally, domain works like this in my games. Almost all areas over 100K will have a Prince. The Prince will then hand out Domain to the Primogen or any other Elders of note. Only in overpopulated cities like Chicago and during the time of the Second Inquisition will EVERY vampire have a domain of some kind.<br /> And even then that's only the Camairlla and Anarchs who can enforce their claims.<br /> <br /> 8. Domain enforcement is not done by the vampire who owns the Domain. It is 90% of the job of the Sheriff and his Deputies. The Scourge has the job of killing any Thin Bloods, Caitiff, or non-affiliated Anarchs that poach.<br /> <br /> 9. Generally, a Sheriff and his Deputies will beat the shit out of you for poaching. You will be only be killed if you're a Thin Blood or Anarch but even the latter isn't 100% if you're known to have friends. Maybe cut your hand off or other non-permanent injury.<br /> <br /> 10. Public Domains with &quot;free hunting&quot; are always in existence in a successful city but these places often find themselves with unusually high amounts of deaths, crime, and missing persons. It's not a great idea to have too many of these places and you have to patrol them vigorously because a Kindred is likely to be messier outside of his place.<br /> <br /> I wonder if I should do another of my TOP TEN TIPS FOR V5 articles on Domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-24-2022, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T12:27:55-08:00","id":1473185,"title":"","content":"A few further points to avoid confusion over some issues - good job by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> for the clarifications:<br /> <br /> - Most elders are by definition embraced from before the 1800s, and most ancillae date to before the 1900s. The social framework of Kindred society as envisioned by the Camarilla doesn't account for the huge changes to cities and to transportation, specifically. It dates to times when there were no blood banks, apartment complexes that provide super-easy feeding, phone and internet to run things from afar, or taxis, subways and airplanes to zip around. Domain and Herd were much more difficult backgrounds to acquire back in the day, what with the smaller number of people, the prevalence of pestilence, the lack of nightlife, and the much lower population density. Assets were concentrated mostly in landed property rather than cash, and even the running of things like merchant companies was done face-to-face on physical location, rather than over the phone or such. Thus, Domain was related in an absolute way to the Resources and Influence backgrounds as well. The result was that the Camarilla elders parcelled out both the cities and the countryside, so that in practice there was no room for new Kindred, many of whom traveled to new lands like the Americas to establish themselves. In the present day, the old concept of Domain falls under the valid criticisms listed here, which is why so many neonates are tempted to go Anarch or join the Sabbat. These two sects suffer from turf wars and from overpopulation, but have much more freedom in operating on a nightly basis than the Camarilla with its feudal domain system.<br /> <br /> - Some elders follow a successful strategy of remaining hidden, and either withdrawing from the Jyhad or operating from behind the scenes. There are several issues here, and also reasons for operating openly instead. Firstly, it is taken as common wisdom in the setting that vampires need to work towards overarching goals and interact with others in order to stave off the Beast and avoid madness. The Embrace introduces monstrous urges, but does not take away the human craving for companionship or new stimuli. Isolated vampires don't end up sitting at home watching TV, they end up like Bulscu, like the Tzimisce's Metamorphosist weirdos, or like the feral Gangrel on the variants of the Road of the Beast. One could make the valid point that vampires who focus on knowledge and scholarship can remain sequestered for long periods of time, but eventually they also need other vampires to fetch further research material.<br /> <br /> - Unless they have strong childer in place, like the Camarilla's Inner Circle do, vampires who conceal themselves become isolated and weak. The elders have their own elders, who have long-term agendas and are not squeamish about discarding useless tools. A vampiric elder knows too much and has too much personal strength to be left alone; in Sins of the Blood, on the chapter on autarkis, it's made clear that one of the Camarilla's goals is to account for all elders and embroil them in a society of mutual pretestation debts. An independent elder like Vlad Tepes is a threat to the leadership of the sects, and is marked for elimination if possible. In all clans, even in the Camarilla, reclusive and 'useless' elders are seen as a waste of blood and are potential diablerie targets for ambitious and more active childer. The Lasombra do this sort of thing openly, but to some extent this happens across the board, as long as the other elders are willing to turn a blind eye. Vampires who tire of playing the games of the sects choose to go into torpor in undisclosed locations, rather than be the target of such plots.<br /> <br /> - It hasn't been pointed out that having a big Domain background, much more than is necessary for a single vampire. is a key stepping stone to establish a brood. When a new vampire is Embraced, the sire typically parcels out a piece of their domain to their progeny, unless that vampire is taking over a vacant domain opened up by the deaths of a lot of vampires after a conflict. Having a lot of Domain means being able to support a lot of childer, which is hugely important in the long term. Vampires who don't want this sort of headache will find themselves outnumbered 10 to 1 by vampires who do establish broods, and all sorts of bad things can happen to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13688-sultanabdal","name":"Sultanabdal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13688_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T13:05:56-08:00","id":1473189,"title":"","content":"As for the rule of thumb of 1 vampire to 100,000 mortals, there are a few things to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> - This is a guideline for the number of vampires who can be supported without them coming into conflict or causing any noticeable ripples under modern day conditions. With this few vampires, the occasional murderous frenzies or corrupt activities are not statistically significant. Cities do end up supporting more vampires than this, but the result is squabbles over turf, and a lot of troubleshooting to take care of the problems that crop up.<br /> <br /> - Tiny princedoms of 4-5 vampires don't really happen, because outside of the major cities, a system of feudal overlordship exists. Many small domains of a few thousand or ten thousand people can fall within the territory of a single vampire, who is subject to a Prince who is based in a relatively larger town. Vampires can have an Elysium in this town but are otherwise spread out over a wide area, unlike the clustered conditions in major cities. Even if the vampire in charge of a minor town has the presumption of calling themselves Prince, they will be outranked by much more formidable vampires and fall under their purview.<br /> <br /> - 1 vampire to 100,000 mortals, even in the ideal case, refers to the number of permanent, established vampires that are present in a city. In practice, there will be many more vampires, with the known but typically unstated fact that most vampires don't make it. Vampires meet the Final Death or are exiled for all sorts of reasons; the Tremere, for example, have a lot of apprentices who fall because they mess up a Thaumaturgy path or ritual, or who are asked to get some difficult ritual ingredients like werewolf fangs or something and understandably fail. Thus, there will be many neonate coteries contrary to the established statistic, but with the unspoken understanding that they will ultimately not be permanent residents of the domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13688-sultanabdal","name":"Sultanabdal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13688_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T13:24:23-08:00","id":1473192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sultanabdal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473189#post1473189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Tiny princedoms of 4-5 vampires don't really happen, because outside of the major cities, a system of feudal overlordship exists. Many small domains of a few thousand or ten thousand people can fall within the territory of a single vampire, who is subject to a Prince who is based in a relatively larger town. Vampires can have an Elysium in this town but are otherwise spread out over a wide area, unlike the clustered conditions in major cities. Even if the vampire in charge of a minor town has the presumption of calling themselves Prince, they will be outranked by much more formidable vampires and fall under their purview..</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should bring this up.<br /> <br /> <b>The Smaller Cities and the Anarchs in my games</b><br /> <br /> I actually note this is where the Anarch &quot;ideal&quot; exists and where the Anarchs exist that cause so much trouble for the Princes since most of them seem to have every advantage compared to the Movement. The Camarilla has a control over the metropolises throughout the world generally but immediately outside of those metropolises, there are often large gangs of Anarchs that pretty much have free reign to do what they want.<br /> <br /> What do I mean by Anarch ideal?<br /> <br /> Outside of New York is Jersey City: Population 261,000 people.<br /> <br /> In the overpopulated, crapsack World of Darkness, let's say that Jersey City has about 12 vampires. In New York, there's a Prince, Primogen, Harpies, Sheriff, Deputies, and Scourge, A whole system of punishment and prestige.<br /> <br /> In Jersey City, there's Dave and his gang. Dave the Anarch Baron and his immediate flunkies, people who he would call his friends, compromise 8-9 vampires that do not need nearly the same amount of feudal bullshit. Dave may be the leader and his friends have a few responsibilities but its a much more informal system and the 3-4 additional vampires don't rock the boat. There's enough in Dave's gang to keep outsiders in check and generally constitute a community even if it's just a large coterie.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs see this as a &quot;solution&quot; to Kindred problems while the Camarilla simply sees it as decentralized government. They don't HAVE to have the complicated Byzantine politics in Bumfuck, Nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-24-2022, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T13:33:19-08:00","id":1473195,"title":"","content":"It's a good idea that the less desirable domains are home to Anarchs and to random vampires in general. While I think there is still very good political material and a strong Camarilla presence over smaller domains (the first Predator and Prey book details a great version over Michigan), the written material naturally gravitates towards major world cities as fundamentally interesting places, rather than study the potentially still juicy interactions in a 'rural' domain. A domain that is dominated by the Gangrel and Nosferatu, where they have to deal with werewolves and the incursions of itinerant Ravnos and nomadic Sabbat packs, would be a refreshing change from the typical setting of Ventrue in skyscrapers and Toreador in art galleries. However, there is a New York by Night, but not a Nebraska by Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13688-sultanabdal","name":"Sultanabdal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13688_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T03:23:08-08:00","id":1473242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sultanabdal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1472936#post1472936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you get down to it, if somebody puts it in their head and takes the time for it, most vampires can be assassinated, hunt or no hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans IRL too, yet assassinations aren't that common even in the most crapsack parts of the world, even in our worst times. Our default state is no violence, for several reasons, including fear of consequence and lack of need/interest.<br /> <br /> I think some people here are too used to how a story works that they forget that no story represents the default state of the setting. There is a story because there is an unusual circumstance.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't live in bunkers because they don't need to live in bunkers. Even with all their paranoia, for most it is a step further to literally think there are ninjas waiting for you in every corner (for a classic VtM game, Arab Ninjas). An elder needs a lot of caution to avoid their enemies, but usually that means avoiding inconvenience, influence theft and the like. Literal attempts on someone's life aren't a frequent occurrence. Not in this sense of not stepping outside home because ninjas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1472962#post1472962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many aspects of V:tM falls apart when you focus in on logistics or logic. Between the ability to have a live in Herd, online banking, the Internet, and video conferences.... there really isn't a reason for a vampire to leave their havens, which in today's world can easily be a converted decommissioned nuclear missile silo or similar military grade secure installation.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the first statement is true, mainly for the Masquerade itself, the rest just isn't.<br /> <br /> There are people that can endure the Lockdown isolation without much of a problem, like yours truly. Even then, if healthy those people still have some contact with the outside world because this is how we get things done and socialize. The game assumes Vampires are the same and there is no reason to believe otherwise. Elders that are <b>really</b> that recluse are also frequently depicted as with extremely low Humanity and risking Wassail because of it, more monsters than people even for the low standards of the Kindred.<br /> <br /> Between socializing with your peers, even to demonstrate you're still not an easy target, dealing with any administrative burdens of your businesses whatever they are, and simply going for a stroll to be acquainted with the city if you ever need to, there's actually no reason for a Vampire of any age to live locked down in a missile silo outside of being in actual torpor, unless it is either a personal preference or they're Survivalists, <b><u>which is a specific mindset no matter how much some of them think everyone else should also be one</u></b>.<br /> <br /> Also, bear in mind there are several ways of being a social creature. Drinkers at a bar aren't less social than high society gadflies, while the complexity and power plays of their socialization may be different. Likewise, the Gangrel are in the end still just as social as any other Vampire despite how different their clan meetings are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473063#post1473063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Domain 5+, probably more like 10-15</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly agree, except by this part depending on how you interpret Domain.<br /> <br /> Having a too big Domain is a sure way to attract enemies and have a lot of work keeping it, so I'd say they can go as low as 2 or 3 unless they specifically want high politic shenanigans with all the risks involved.<br /> <br /> Unless you mean some of those dots meaning Domain by Proxy with their allies and lessers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473159#post1473159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short the Backgrounds system is based in abstraction rather than simulation, this is great for book keeping, but troublesome for figuring out what applies to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet it seems to me that you're being too simulationist in your interpretation, using the concrete examples of what the BGs do to make them give benefits they're not meant to, instead of focusing on their actual goals.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Resources</b></u> means money. While you can be the owner of a Hospital, as a Resource it matters only as a source of income. You can use it to bribe your way through law and rules, but just as with actual money it isn't any form of automatic access. Hospital owners don't have any kind of free access to shit on the rules just because they literally own the place, and trying to do so may have unforeseen consequences.<br /> <br /> Why? Because you only have <i>Resources</i>, so you're not entitled to free access to blood. Indeed, you're not even entitled to hold Domain over your own hospital under Kindred law, if you have no Domain of yourself the rules for feeding in your own hospital may not be that clear-cut or even benefit you.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Herd</u></b> means stable and safe access to blood sources, regardless of how this access works. If you have already a system in place at your hospital to be able to feed on patients, this <u><b>is</b></u> <i>Herd</i>. If you don't have <i>Herd</i>, then this system isn't guaranteed, it still needs work to safeguard it against common problems. It isn't that it doesn't work, but it only works as much as bribing your way would work in any situation anyway, but leave a trail of evidence.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Domain</u></b> means lordship over an area under Kindred eyes. For whatever reason most Vampires will recognize your authority over that area and there will be less of a need for you to personally enforce it all the time. If other vampires accept you're the owner of the hospital and don't mess with it or feed there without your consent, that <b><u>is</u></b> <i>Domain</i>. If you don't have <i>Domain</i>, then other Kindred do not recognize your authority over it despite you being owed its revenue. It is either in someone else's territory, closed to everyone by the Prince's decree, including you, or free for all to use. You can try to leverage your ownership of the building on those matters, and it may help, indeed, but ultimately yours is not the last word and you'll have to play by someone else's rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sultanabdal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473195#post1473195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the written material naturally gravitates towards major world cities as fundamentally interesting places, rather than study the potentially still juicy interactions in a 'rural' domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a sad side-effect of the Punk ethos of the game, as both as a literary genre, philosophy and aesthetics the Punk movement is greatly focused on large urbanization for good and ill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T04:51:50-08:00","id":1473246,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473156#post1473156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elders are flawed individuals, whose actions are not always perfectly rational. They're just older, more powerful, more entrenched. More <i>entitled</i>. They may even delude themselves into thinking they're better than the Neonates scrambling for sustenance in the slums. But they're just another parasite.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is so well said that I'm mad I didn't say it (I now want to steal it; grant permission for me to quote you in the book that'll be released.... I really am misusing the word &quot;soon&quot; aren't I?) <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As CTPhipps said, having control over a hospital or blood bank IS having dots Herd and/or Domain. If I were the Storyteller in charge, that is absolutely how I would rule it.<br /> </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Having control over a hospital or blood bank should require a minimum number of dots. A small hospital would be Domain 2, Herd 2 at the very least (and you're probably going to need extra dots for domain security)<br /> <br /> A blood bank is different. I think you'd use your own background. <br /> <br /> <br /> Herd is a kinda messy background because it's ruled like you're looking for free-range meals when the term &quot;herd&quot; naturally suggests you're going to eat caged dinners. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T06:25:21-08:00","id":1473253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473173#post1473173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We may be talking about different things. I suppose my only point is we are never universal so you can't really say how every elder will feel, act, or spend his resources. I agree with priorities changing as we get older, but some work for love of whatever, never caring about the paycheck. I look at older (65+) people, some want to sit in front of the tv all day, some want to stay active outdoors, some still go to bars or restaurants to socialize most nights, some want to spend their days with family, some hang out with younger generations to stay young themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, individuality and personal preference will always be present, but I think the part that is being overlooked is that the WoD setting exerts a form of social Darwinism when it comes to its various splats. The brutality of the setting culls those who are the poorly adapted to it or refuse to adopt new methods of behavior according to the situation.<br /> <br /> I am thinking of the generals in WWI who had no idea that armies having machine guns meant their Napolean era techniques were out of date and thus ordered their troops to charge such emplacements without cover. <br /> <br /> The attrition of those who can't adapt, who can't read the changes around them, ensures that almost no one who exists long enough to be an active Elder will have behaviors that will contribute to a lack of power in such an environment.<br /> <br /> V:tM as a game says you can make any kind of character you want. V:tM as a setting says only the strong and paranoid survive. It reminds me of a quote attributed to Henry Ford, &quot;Any customer can have a car painted any color, as long as it is black&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T06:49:56-08:00","id":1473256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sultanabdal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473189#post1473189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rule of thumb of 1 vampire to 100,000 mortals, there are a few things to keep in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the issues is that in previous editions the 1/100,000 rule was used to explicitly state a maximum vampire population. This covered every vampire in total, as in those who are awake, those in torpor, those in other dimensions, those that isolated themselves from vampire society, and finally it included the Kuei-Jin. The KotE vampires made up about a third of the total vampire population.<br /> <br /> Assuming the ratio still holds, with 7.5 billion mortals on the planet that means there are about 75,000 vampires in existence. Of those about 25,000 are going to be Kuei-Jin vampires. The remaining 50,000 vampires in the world are cainites and when you start running the numbers on how vampire society is supposed to work, the entire setting changes tone real fast.<br /> <br /> Using a Camarilla city social design for the sake of simplicity and discussion, if you assume that the 6 major clans are represented, the prince pulls double duty as their clans Primogen, and that the Princes clan will have more members than other clans just out of bias, then the city can easily hit a vampire population of 40+ vampires and that is before we discuss clans or bloodlines which wouldn't have a Primogen existing in the same city, so that number could easily hit almost 100 vampires in a city. But when you remember that there is an up limit to total vampire population, that means if you divide the vampires up into such large city groups and spread them across the world, then vampires would be incredibly rare. Like only a few cities per state would have vampires.<br /> <br /> But all of that is assuming that every vampire is awake and an active part of kindred society. Factor in the those in torpor, those that have isolated themselves, or those who travel rather than maintaining a permanent home, and those numbers fall fairly fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T07:19:58-08:00","id":1473258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473242#post1473242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly agree, except by this part depending on how you interpret Domain.<br /> <br /> Having a too big Domain is a sure way to attract enemies and have a lot of work keeping it, so I'd say they can go as low as 2 or 3 unless they specifically want high politic shenanigans with all the risks involved.<br /> <br /> Unless you mean some of those dots meaning Domain by Proxy with their allies and lessers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of all the bells and whistles you can add to a Domain to make it really expensive. I was also, subconsciously, thinking of a lair, rather than just a hunting ground. I'd imagine that if an Elder had a hunting ground it would be the equivalent of a younger groups one.<br /> <br /> My point overall was that most Elders, and certainly the succesful ones, are going to accrue a lot of resources over the years, whereas most STs simply concentrate on their disciplines and handwave the rest away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T07:21:18-08:00","id":1473259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473242#post1473242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet it seems to me that you're being too simulationist in your interpretation, using the concrete examples of what the BGs do to make them give benefits they're not meant to, instead of focusing on their actual goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The backgrounds as written are like saying a &quot;knife is designed to cut&quot; but due to its over simplicity it fails to cover the idea that a Chef's Knife, a Butter knife, and a Surgeon's scalpel all fall under the definition of &quot;knife&quot;. Many butter knives are dull and have blunted tips, so trying to cut cold butter can be an awkward task, good luck trying to use one in a meaningful way in combat. <br /> <br /> Your interpretation basically treats backgrounds, if we follow the knife metaphor, as a chef's knife, but it can't be used for anything but preparing food and can't be used outside of a kitchen. Resources as a background allows you to do anything that having money lets you do, not just buy specific things or used in specific ways. <br /> <br /> In my opinion, it is not a question of being simulationist vs. abstractionist, but instead many STs and Players not thinking ramifications through and thus greatly limit their games potential.<br /> <br /> Your take on Resources is particularly egregious in this respect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473242#post1473242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Resources</b></u> means money. While you can be the owner of a Hospital, as a Resource it matters only as a source of income. You can use it to bribe your way through law and rules, but just as with actual money it isn't any form of automatic access. Hospital owners don't have any kind of free access to shit on the rules just because they literally own the place, and trying to do so may have unforeseen consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you own the hospital, that means you set policy, you tell the hospital how to spend its money, which departments are created, which ones are shut down, what research will be allowed. As long as nothing blatantly breaks the laws or violates standards, no one will pay attention to what you are doing.<br /> <br /> Your way of thinking would be like suggesting that owning an expensive car gives no benefit other than being able to drive. Owning a 100K sports car will have an effect on your dating/hunting, owning a classic car will allow access to those in the car enthusiast circles, owning a nascar would allow your ghoul driver to participate in races, etc. etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T09:25:56-08:00","id":1473269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473259#post1473259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The backgrounds as written are like saying a &quot;knife is designed to cut&quot; but due to its over simplicity it fails to cover the idea that a Chef's Knife, a Butter knife, and a Surgeon's scalpel all fall under the definition of &quot;knife&quot;. Many butter knives are dull and have blunted tips, so trying to cut cold butter can be an awkward task, good luck trying to use one in a meaningful way in combat.<br /> <br /> Your interpretation basically treats backgrounds, if we follow the knife metaphor, as a chef's knife, but it can't be used for anything but preparing food and can't be used outside of a kitchen. Resources as a background allows you to do anything that having money lets you do, not just buy specific things or used in specific ways.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, it is not a question of being simulationist vs. abstractionist, but instead many STs and Players not thinking ramifications through and thus greatly limit their games potential.<br /> <br /> Your take on Resources is particularly egregious in this respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Chef's Knife does more than preparing food, then it's more than just a prop and needs Weapons rules. It could be represented in the game as a Knife providing a bonus to cook and a penalty to attack rolls (or having a penalty to attack and/or dmage, and treating as fluff when making food. It's besides the point). These two things, however, are sepparate: The rules to cook and the rules to attack are different rules.<br /> <br /> It may be counter-intuitive, but I would say that's how Backgrounds are built: Not as &quot;knife is designed to cut&quot;, but as &quot;this cuts, it may be a knife&quot;.<br /> <br /> The most clear example it's with Influence. In our world there are few examples of influence w/o resources or viceversa - either one can buy influence, or one can use existing influence over <i>any </i>segment of society to gain money ... Yet it's abstracted in the game system as separate Traits, you can have one without the other as much as you can have Strength w/o Stamina (more so, actually).<br /> <br /> I would say that in these cases the burden of explanation it's on the player that buys the dots, not the ST. You would have to explain where your money comes from that it doesn't traduce in any sort of influence, or why are you extremely poor with that amount of Influence...That is: The Concept determines the Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> That way, it's not so much that the owner of a hospital can't have an advantage over &quot;hunting&quot; there (IOC), but rather that to represent &quot;owner of a hospital&quot; in such a way, you would need (OOC) to buy or earn several Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> That's what, I think, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> it's going on when she says that &quot;<i>While you can be the owner of a Hospital, as a Resource it matters only as a source of income. </i>&quot; If that doesn't make any sense ... well, that would just mean having dots in Resources <i>only </i>ain't enough to represent that concept very well.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could leverage one to get the other &quot;in game&quot;, like with any Background. Using the appropiate skills and interpretation you can leverage that sum of money that's being delivered to you into realizing the concept. And that's where the &quot;unforeseen consequences&quot; could come into place<br /> <br /> Like, say, the hospital you want to buy could be under the Domain of another vampire, that doesn't care about owning the hospital because he has other sources of blood and better things to do that buying every hospital in the area - but *would* care about you owning it because he knows that his &quot;vampiric rigths&quot; over the place can be leveraged over your character, and could be questioned by rivals if he doesn't leverage them. Or maybe the hospital you bought was being eyed by another vampire, that in a fit of paranoia interprets your move as an attack. Or maybe it's haunted, a Giovanni can help but it would cost. Unjust serendipity? Hey, it's a <i>Roleplaying Game</i>: shenanigans ensue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-25-2022, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:10:59-08:00","id":1473280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473269#post1473269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, say, the hospital you want to buy could be under the Domain of another vampire, that doesn't care about owning the hospital because he has other sources of blood and better things to do that buying every hospital in the area - but *would* care about you owning it because he knows that his &quot;vampiric rigths&quot; over the place can be leveraged over your character, and could be questioned by rivals if he doesn't leverage them. Or maybe the hospital you bought was being eyed by another vampire, that in a fit of paranoia interprets your move as an attack. Or maybe it's haunted, a Giovanni can help but it would cost. Unjust serendipity? Hey, it's a <i>Roleplaying Game</i>: shenanigans ensue</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you are saying about story hooks, but at the same time those story hooks only function if the people essentially railroad the options for how things are done.<br /> <br /> Just for simplicity let us stick with Resources for the moment. Take Resources 5 at character generation, which means you can create any back story about how your money was made and how you continue to make it. Then you explain how your characters portfolio is laid out. All of this is session zero basics where the player and ST work out all the bugs.<br /> <br /> So thanks to Resources 5, that means you can buy an empty plot of land and build a hospital just as easily as taking over and existing hospital. This doesn't mean much in most games, but it means the storyhook about another vampire being interested in the hospital doesn't really work if you are building it from scratch. Like wise since you are choosing where to build it, that means you can research who else is in the area and would there be a conflict. Yes this destroys a potential plot hook, but in truth is so basic it is like checking the local zoning laws to see if your project would be prohibited.<br /> <br /> Lastly one of the biggest benefits with something like Resources 5 is that it creates a scenario where the standard interactions break down or out right don't happen. For instance just because you own a piece of property, doesn't mean that your name is on a plaque or there is a statue of you in the entry way. There is no requirement that everyone automatically knows every financial interaction.<br /> <br /> Combat between two melee builds means they see each other, they are within arms reach of each other to do or recieve damage. This can be augmented by things like the environment or disciplines like Obfuscate. But over all the parameters for the conflict are set like a stage or arena.<br /> <br /> Conflict using Resources or other Backgrounds is more like an online 4 way chess match. The attacks, defenses, or other interactions are non-localized.<br /> <br /> A combat statted Brujah might claim domain over an apartment building they have a haven in, but a Ventrue with Resources 5 can just contact the owners of the building and buy it or just dominate the transfer of ownership. At which time every tenet is given an eviction notice. The Brujah loses their Domain and their Haven in one move.<br /> <br /> Now the typical Brujah role play answer is to go and punch the Ventrue in the face until you get your haven back. But this line of thinking doesn't explain how the Brujah knows who to punch. The Ventrue can own a holding company, which own other companies, which in turn other companies, which in turn bought this building. Most of those businesses are shell corporations or only exist on paper, but if you spread them out so they are based outside the city, state, or perhaps country, only a character with a background in that level of business would be able to detect your involvement if at all. It is possible that the Brujah might have a contact who could find this out, but let's be honest here, most vampires don't have access to fortune 500 grade forensic accountants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T12:33:33-08:00","id":1473292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473246#post1473246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is so well said that I'm mad I didn't say it (I now want to steal it; grant permission for me to quote you in the book that'll be released.... I really am misusing the word &quot;soon&quot; aren't I?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You have my blessing to use the line however you see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T22:21:07-08:00","id":1473317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473258#post1473258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking of all the bells and whistles you can add to a Domain to make it really expensive. I was also, subconsciously, thinking of a lair, rather than just a hunting ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally forgot that you could use dots in Domain to add shenanigans to it instead of increasing size. I stand corrected and agree with you entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473280#post1473280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you are saying about story hooks, but at the same time those story hooks only function if the people essentially railroad the options for how things are done.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you didn't get it. You're still focusing on what you know about money and property and how to game them instead of looking at what the game trait does as a game trait.<br /> <br /> \u200bBy the way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> got it right, indeed.<br /> <br /> <b>As a game trait</b>, <i>Resources</i> means money. Property, jobs, income, all of those are the means for your trait to materialize in the fiction of the game, but the trait in you sheet is <i>Resources</i> all the same.<br /> <br /> Can you use it to declare you own a hospital at character creation? Unless the ST veto it, yes. That gives you some degree of power over how this hospital works? Yes, it is your property, you don't need other traits to own your property.<br /> <br /> So, you did your research to chose a hospital you can control completely without serious conflicts with other kindred? <b><u>Buy <i>Domain</i> to represent this</u></b>. Your <b>trait</b> does not cover that benefit.<br /> <br /> What that means in practical terms, though?<br /> <br /> You certainly can still hunt at your own hospital if you only have <i>Resources</i>, it is just that you <b><u>don't</u></b> have such a reliable safety on doing so. Most of your staff don't know a thing about you and see no reason to let you break protocol. Security cameras won't be turned off for you unless you give some pressure that will raise questions. Vampires that weren't interested in the area before may now want to claim it as Domain <i>because of the hospital</i>, and it may be granted because you don't have such a claim already to defend.<br /> <br /> In general, you can use your hospital since it is your property, but benefits that go beyond being a source of income aren't guaranteed to be there without work, to be reliable or be consistent. Because that's what <i>Herd </i>and <i>Domain</i> are: not just things you have, but things you have that work in a certain way consistently and reliably.<br /> <br /> For the matter of how you describe your properties at character creation: you <b>don't</b> have that complete freedom. In the same way that you can't use the description of your Stamina to justify deriving the benefits of Appearance or Strength from it, you can't just say that the description of your property let you derive the benefits of other BGs from <i>Resources</i>. If you only have trait X, then only the benefits of trait X are yours by right. If you think your hospital should give you more, then it should be more than one trait in your sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T09:18:03-08:00","id":1473338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473317#post1473317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You certainly can still hunt at your own hospital if you only have <i>Resources</i>, it is just that you <b><u>don't</u></b> have such a reliable safety on doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Following that logic, if you use Resources to buy a house, while you may be able to sleep there, you can't call it a Haven.<br /> <br /> Another thing that you seem to be struggling with is the separation between hunting and feeding. If you have a cooler full of blood packs in your car, you don't roll to hunt them down, at most you just find a private location to drink them. If you own the hospital or blood bank, the blood is already in your possession. There is nothing to hunt. Hence why Domain isn't as good a fit as you believe it to be.<br /> <br /> Now I have mentioned previously in the thread that perhaps a subsystem for Backgrounds that might clean this up would be requiring a certain mix of backgrounds and levels to have something like a hospital, so I am not opposed to it taking more than Resources. But at the end of the day both Backgrounds can gain you access to a hospital, but each has its own pros and cons, which fits a role play game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T10:09:34-08:00","id":1473341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473338#post1473338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Following that logic, if you use Resources to buy a house, while you may be able to sleep there, you can't call it a Haven.<br /> <br /> Another thing that you seem to be struggling with is the separation between hunting and feeding. If you have a cooler full of blood packs in your car, you don't roll to hunt them down, at most you just find a private location to drink them. If you own the hospital or blood bank, the blood is already in your possession. There is nothing to hunt. Hence why Domain isn't as good a fit as you believe it to be.<br /> <br /> Now I have mentioned previously in the thread that perhaps a subsystem for Backgrounds that might clean this up would be requiring a certain mix of backgrounds and levels to have something like a hospital, so I am not opposed to it taking more than Resources. But at the end of the day both Backgrounds can gain you access to a hospital, but each has its own pros and cons, which fits a role play game.</div> </div> </div> </div>How I handle it in my 20 years of gaming is like this and this subject has come up before:<br /> <br /> With Resources as a background, you can have a house and a mansion as well as customize them to the level you are able to afford to. I treat HAVEN as a background differently because if you buy that, you don't need to have the Resources and you have what I call, &quot;permission to be a goddamned supervillain.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you buy Haven then you can and should basically customize it to the level that sounds every bit as bizarre as some of my players want: &quot;Yes, I live in the Sewers. However, I live in an abandoned Subway Station that has been turned into a Edwardian mansion with its own private dojo and stolen super computer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Abandoned amusement parks, secret laboratories, and so on. I also make note that even if you own a hospital, it's not quite the all-you-can-eat buffet you may think. Feeding one vampire off blood? Sure, absolutely, but a vampire needs the equivalent of a trasnfusion of a pint of blood every day so that's 365 pints of blood per year and that's the minimum.<br /> <br /> Vampires can't actually feed exclusively off the blood in a hospital, at least all of the ones in a city, without that becoming VERY apparent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T10:49:52-08:00","id":1473344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473341#post1473341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How I handle it in my 20 years of gaming is like this and this subject has come up before:<br /> <br /> With Resources as a background, you can have a house and a mansion as well as customize them to the level you are able to afford to. I treat HAVEN as a background differently because if you buy that, you don't need to have the Resources and you have what I call, &quot;permission to be a goddamned supervillain.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you buy Haven then you can and should basically customize it to the level that sounds every bit as bizarre as some of my players want: &quot;Yes, I live in the Sewers. However, I live in an abandoned Subway Station that has been turned into a Edwardian mansion with its own private dojo and stolen super computer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Abandoned amusement parks, secret laboratories, and so on. I also make note that even if you own a hospital, it's not quite the all-you-can-eat buffet you may think. Feeding one vampire off blood? Sure, absolutely, but a vampire needs the equivalent of a trasnfusion of a pint of blood every day so that's 365 pints of blood per year and that's the minimum.<br /> <br /> Vampires can't actually feed exclusively off the blood in a hospital, at least all of the ones in a city, without that becoming VERY apparent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your way seems imbalanced to me.<br /> <br /> If you have a haven, you can't really kit it out, specialize, or put things that would augment your power. But if you take Haven as a Background then you get all the extras as a bonus. Following that line of thinking, if your character picks up a wad of cash or a gold bar they have Resources, but if they take Resources as a background then won't it grant them all the benefits as well? You are essentially making a split tier system for no reason.<br /> <br /> I get the concept of stuff that is purchased is more important to the player, or to be more precise have a degree of storyline immunity. But if you are going to focus on that, every background should have something to that degree. What is your example of &quot;permission to be a goddamned supervillain&quot; grade Resources?<br /> <br /> As far as transfusions go, yes having one patient needing 365 infusions a year would be quite suspicious. On the other hand if you own the hospital then the concept of having multiple fake patient files to obfuscate who is getting how much blood isn't exactly a 4th dimensional chess move. You could also forge paperwork so every surgery uses an extra blood pack or two and the excess is sent elsewhere.<br /> <br /> If you really want a deep cover, then you designate an entire wing of the hospital to long term care/coma patients that only a specialty team works with. Harvest the patients for blood and occasionally have blood packs sent up. In a weird way this can be an interesting way of maintaining humanity for a medically minded kindred. Rather than kill mortal enemies, they just induce a coma and give the surviving family members the good news that your coma wing has a charity willing to pay the bills for upkeep. If you are less humane you only pay part of the upkeep bills, which means you end up getting paid Resources by the family to get free blood from the coma patient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T11:11:11-08:00","id":1473345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473344#post1473344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a haven, you can't really kit it out, specialize, or put things that would augment your power. But if you take Haven as a Background then you get all the extras as a bonus. Following that line of thinking, if your character picks up a wad of cash or a gold bar they have Resources, but if they take Resources as a background then won't it grant them all the benefits as well? You are essentially making a split tier system for no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bluntly, I think you misunderstood the point. If you have Resources 5 and you have the time, energy, and willingness to risk crime then you could build a underground sewer lair.<br /> <br /> However, that might use up all of your millions to do it and would require roleplaying all of the various things you'd have to do to do it.<br /> <br /> With Haven, you just do it.<br /> <br /> A vampire who doesn't have millions can also have something money CAN'T buy, which is a lot. Hence why I said the supervillain lair.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with STs who want to have a shark tank to feed people for just Resources and don't need the Haven but I don't mind that there's a Resource specifically for people who want to have their home rigged with secret passages and explosives.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T11:24:44-08:00","id":1473347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473344#post1473344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> As far as transfusions go, yes having one patient needing 365 infusions a year would be quite suspicious. On the other hand if you own the hospital then the concept of having multiple fake patient files to obfuscate who is getting how much blood isn't exactly a 4th dimensional chess move. You could also forge paperwork so every surgery uses an extra blood pack or two and the excess is sent elsewhere.<br /> <br /> If you really want a deep cover, then you designate an entire wing of the hospital to long term care/coma patients that only a specialty team works with. Harvest the patients for blood and occasionally have blood packs sent up. In a weird way this can be an interesting way of maintaining humanity for a medically minded kindred. Rather than kill mortal enemies, they just induce a coma and give the surviving family members the good news that your coma wing has a charity willing to pay the bills for upkeep. If you are less humane you only pay part of the upkeep bills, which means you end up getting paid Resources by the family to get free blood from the coma patient.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where the plot armor comes in for Herd and Domain. If you just own the hospital without herd and domain people will notice and they will turn you in. On the other hand if the hospital administrator is your retainer, and you have domain 4 hospital, and herd 3 from hospital, the organization is paid for and set up to be in place to cover things up with fake paperwork and people who look the other way at your comings and goings and blood theft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T11:27:34-08:00","id":1473348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473347#post1473347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is where the plot armor comes in for Herd and Domain. If you just own the hospital without herd and domain people will notice and they will turn you in. On the other hand if the hospital administrator is your retainer, and you have domain 4 hospital, and herd 3 from hospital, the organization is paid for and set up to be in place to cover things up with fake paperwork and people who look the other way at your comings and goings and blood theft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, I do think a lot of flexibility is needed from an ST. Its better to give more Resources than nickel and dime players over what they can do. Also, making Resources in-game should not require Experience, IMHO.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T18:23:00-08:00","id":1473370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473345#post1473345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bluntly, I think you misunderstood the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, hence why I asked you to explain Bond Villian grade Resources. Because you are not making sense. Either you are enforcing the RAW equally across backgrounds, or you are making home brew. The way you explained your take on it is hopping from one to the other and back again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473345#post1473345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have Resources 5 and you have the time, energy, and willingness to risk crime then you could build a underground sewer lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does crime have to do with it? Resources 5 means you can drop a couple million on refurbishing a nuclear bunker legally. Heck you can buy entire ghost towns legally. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473345#post1473345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, that might use up all of your millions to do it and would require roleplaying all of the various things you'd have to do to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resources 5 covers millions, billions, and given the fluff regarding how individual vampires are richer than any human also Trillions.<br /> <br /> This is why I say there is a fundamental disconnect with many STs &amp; Players when it comes to moving a V:tM game from Lost Boys street level games to something with a broader scope, even if the story is contained in just one city.<br /> <br /> After a certain point the mechanics shift, so on a street level game you would use firearms to shoot your enemies and Resources to buy ammo. In broader scope games (need a better descriptor) your attack method is how you use your Resources as ammo rather than buying ammo. I get the idea of knee capping some backgrounds at street level play, but those home brew ideas fall apart if applied to non-street level games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T07:33:13-08:00","id":1473405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473338#post1473338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you own the hospital or blood bank, the blood is already in your possession. There is nothing to hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have no idea of how a hospital actually works, does you?<br /> <br /> Or any business by that matter, because thinking that you can dispose of every single asset of the business as if it was just your personal property is A) frequently illegal, B) always noticeable and C) the easiest way to end up without it for being a terrible manager.<br /> <br /> \u200bFirst, there's what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24221\" data-vbnamecard=\"24221\">Vamps Like Us</a> said in post #43. Basically, your reasoning on how you can set up the entire system in your hospital to execute and cover up the embezzlement of blood is exactly what <i>Herd</i> does here. That's what I was trying to say this entire time: if you only have <i>Resources</i>, you have to describe this scheme, you have to dedicate time <i><u>and rolls</u></i> to the scheme, and at any point a new complication to your scheme may appear.<br /> <br /> Without <i>Domain</i> it is specially dangerous because other vampires have no reason to not interfere if they find out, unless again you step out of your way to take precautions, meet the interested parties to negotiate, put in general a lot of personal effort and political capital into making it work, still risking setbacks and deals with unreasonable parties.<br /> <br /> If you buy <i>Herd</i>, it directly represents your scheme and it is already well enough established that no further action is needed for it to be there and be reasonably safe. The ST may put it in the line as a story seed here and there, but generally you're entitled to take it for granted. If you buy <i>Domain</i> then likewise other vampires already recognize it and things are reasonably settled down. Unless some major political setback affects you, your authority over the hospital isn't questioned and the reasons for this may remain mostly as background instead of taking your play time and risk failure on dice rolls.<br /> <br /> Keeping your hospital as a safe personal space and blood source while just buying <i>Resources </i>will cost you a lot and be always at risk. It is a time and effort that most players would prefer to invest somewhere else in the game. The ST may give you some leeway depending on how it impacts or not the game, but you're not entitled to expect that. You should at least expect a roll from time to time to see if some problem comes up that wouldn't if it was properly a Background of that kind in your sheet.<br /> <br /> Not to say that while it is a poor attitude to mess with a player's traits frequently or without good reason on the ST's part, the PC actively putting their traits at risk for a greater gain is another matter entirely. By setting up such a scheme in your hospital without the backing of BGs meant for giving the benefits you're after, you're putting the company and your <i>Resources</i> at risk. A bad series of rolls or excessive abuse of this scheme could perfectly justify the PC ending up with mounting costs, frozen assets, and a series of other setbacks that could effectively harm their <i>Resources</i> rating directly. temporarily or even permanently.<br /> <br /> Because businesses, companies, etc. including hospitals are very complex things to manage and keep lucrative, and while schemes in them certainly exist, they do have risks and costs. While most rich people involved in schemes are probably off the hooks, that's because they do put the effort and capital to make it work, which would be represented in game either by dots in other BGs or by investing play time so to speak. And even then, every year there's a number of rich people all around the world suffering serious setbacks or even facing harsh consequences for it. They're not a majority, but they're there to show you that it isn't a guaranteed thing.<br /> <br /> The greatest reason to not be so secure in such an arrangement, though, is simply fairness with your players. <i>Resources</i>, <i>Domain</i> and <i>Herd</i> are all traits with equal costs, and are there to make for different character concepts. If you make one such character concept objectively stronger than the others by making it access the benefits of the others by default, even if just at high levels, then either your group will be extremely uniform, or there's a big chance that there will be some resentment from the players with the &quot;weaker&quot; concepts, and with reason. This is not about what money can buy, but about what the actual resources the <b><i>players</i></b> have, dots, can buy, and that they feel the end result of their expenditure as fair and fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T08:13:57-08:00","id":1473407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473405#post1473405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because businesses, companies, etc. including hospitals are very complex things to manage and keep lucrative, and while schemes in them certainly exist, they do have risks and costs. While most rich people involved in schemes are probably off the hooks, that's because they do put the effort and capital to make it work, which would be represented in game either by dots in other BGs or by investing play time so to speak. And even then, every year there's a number of rich people all around the world suffering serious setbacks or even facing harsh consequences for it. They're not a majority, but they're there to show you that it isn't a guaranteed thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I view high Resources as also having the associated personnel required to operate the trust fund/business/company/globe-spanning organization, but obviously they are all regular mortals and not part of any vamp circle. This is mostly because it's not at all a fun rpg element to manage a business, and usually the vamp is the beneficiary/owner/shareholder rather than the CEO. Unless, of course, it's part of a story where the characters' Resources are under threat.<br /> <br /> You make an excellent point about background dots being equally valuable. Players and STs often lose sight of that and make Resources the most 'powerful' background when it should be the same as the others. I'll certainly bear this in mind for the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T08:49:34-08:00","id":1473468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473407#post1473407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I view high Resources as also having the associated personnel required to operate the trust fund/business/company/globe-spanning organization, but obviously they are all regular mortals and not part of any vamp circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do that too as a rule of thumb, it is just that a CEO's worst nightmare is a meddling owner that can't stop asking to use the company's assets as if they were their own, with the CEO being torn between denying their effective boss or doing stupid decisions to comply with the meddler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T10:40:49-08:00","id":1473478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473405#post1473405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have no idea of how a hospital actually works, does you?<br /> <br /> Or any business by that matter, because thinking that you can dispose of every single asset of the business as if it was just your personal property is A) frequently illegal, B) always noticeable and C) the easiest way to end up without it for being a terrible manager.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so you are going with a personal attack stacked with a bunch of business-related platitudes that are great in theory but hold little to no relevance in real life business. If you are going with useless non-sense could you at least make it relevant?<br /> <br /> You seem to be operating under the concept that an <b><u>Owner</u></b> is the same thing as a <b><u>manager</u></b>. A common misconception for someone whose business experience is limited to managerial or lower positions. To be fair no one would expect a clerk to understand how the Owners conduct business on a large scale. Part of the reason they have business classes. As an IRL business owner I have to say that those classes are okay for theoretical knowledge, but very poor when it comes to practical application when it comes to business.<br /> <br /> A manager can make business decisions on the day to day activities of said business. Which workers are scheduled for what shifts, who shifts jobs on the fly if a problem arises, etc. But a Manager can't decide to close the business or sell off its assets. At most they can suggest to terminate a worker or resign their own postion.<br /> <br /> An Owner can do all of those things and more. If the business as served its purpose, you can close it and sell it off for profit. You could likewise expand it by investing more into the business or creating branch sites. You can change the direction of the business to suit current trends or choose to hold fast to a traditional business model.<br /> <br /> Owning a hospital is no different than owning a supermarket or running a factory. You own it, you have specialists in your employ, and you decide which direction the business goes in as far as research, development, or product development.<br /> <br /> You are imagining board meetings, committee hearings, public forums, or stock holders meetings. When you have a business model that is based off of single ownership, all of that goes away. Sure you might have manager grade personnel on site, but their function is to enforce you directives, rather than enforce the stock holders directives.<br /> <br /> Though out history there are many examples of very wealthy people owning newspapers, and despite those papers having all the journalists, the editors, and desk chiefs, the owner can say &quot;we will not cover that subject&quot; or this paper will support &quot;this ideology&quot; in its daily news coverage. Which is their right as the owner of the paper.<br /> <br /> Remember that we are talking about WoD here, which is supposed to be our world if only a bit darker, a bit more corrupt, and a bit harsher. So if it is happening IRL then that is a base line for the game setting, it can't by definition exceed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T11:42:35-08:00","id":1473484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473478#post1473478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so you are going with a personal attack stacked with a bunch of business-related platitudes that are great in theory but hold little to no relevance in real life business. If you are going with useless non-sense could you at least make it relevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the first, you are right. That was not an adequate opening, I let my frustration (with many things) speak for me at the time and I shouldn't. I'm sorry about that, but I didn't edit out either as it was your right to answer it. I'll edit it out or let it in place as you wish in this particular matter.<br /> <br /> For the second part, I made my actual arguments from the third paragraph onward, so you basically ignored everything I actually said. Since you were possibly and rightfully angry at me still, I won't hold that against you if you want to reread the rest of the post to make an actual answer to it.<br /> <br /> And on the matter of the rest of your post, you completely missed my point. You said nothing I don't know or understand, or that I hadn't considered in my post. You also must take care with the assumption that <i>Resources </i>5 always means the same relationship with the business, because this character may either be an investor to whom that hospital is just a small percentage of their properties or someone whose only business is that hospital, and you can't decide that alone without ST approval. Other games (namely, Mage) have rules to specify where on the range of richness you are, but without it no Background should be enough to define things that may come to affect the setting as the ST intends to use it.<br /> <br /> It really seems to me that by being a business owner yourself you like exactly to give <i>Resources</i> a punch the game never intended for it because of hoe much you understand it IRL. But the question isn't what a business does IRL, is what a trait does in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T12:29:31-08:00","id":1473490,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't rule resources 5 as billions (unless we're talking weak currency here) Backgrounds 5+ are available in the WoD, even if they're not talked about much in vampire corebooks. <br /> <br /> I see the resources background primarily as not what you own, but what you can do with it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Very few vampires work for a living, they might busy themselves with work related projects, they might personally steal quite a bit, but they do these things on a foundation built and managed by others. Vampires either own stuff or they control people who own stuff, and they let their money work for them. Baring a few defects, any neonate who knows how to blood bond can easily join the ranks of the bourgeoisie If one of their proxies ends up in massive debt, it's very easy for a vampire to cut them loose. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After a certain point the mechanics shift, so on a street level game you would use firearms to shoot your enemies and Resources to buy ammo </div> </div> </div>This point is like... resources 1. Unless we're talking machineguns or cannons or equipping an entire posse the ammunition isn't expensive. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With Resources as a background, you can have a house and a mansion as well as customize them to the level you are able to afford to. I treat HAVEN as a background differently because if you buy that, you don't need to have the Resources and you have what I call, &quot;permission to be a goddamned supervillain.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Haven shouldn't be a background, unless we're talking chantries with labs and occult libraries and other such facilities. <br /> If you want something real cool it'd be like... Resources + Larceny. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T13:15:13-08:00","id":1473495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473478#post1473478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Owning a hospital is no different than owning a supermarket or running a factory. You own it, you have specialists in your employ, and you decide which direction the business goes in as far as research, development, or product development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is where we disagree the most. Owning a hospital and using it as a blood buffet is quite different than owning a supermarket and grabbing a frozen pizza. It is regulated, inspected, inventoried, etc... The employees are more likely to take a moral stand on illegal actions. Doctors and nurses have license's, there is a higher income and education level in general for employees, thus harder to bribe or convince to look the other way. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T13:44:40-08:00","id":1473496,"title":"","content":"IRL a LOT of blood that goes to a blood bank is wasted due to blood not having a great shelf life and supply/demand being inconsistent. It really probably isn't so hard for a few dozen bags to be written off each month, depending on the size of the bank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T14:03:22-08:00","id":1473497,"title":"","content":"I remember when Resources 5 = 5 million dollars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473496#post1473496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IRL a LOT of blood that goes to a blood bank is wasted due to blood not having a great shelf life and supply/demand being inconsistent. It really probably isn't so hard for a few dozen bags to be written off each month, depending on the size of the bank.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the way that you can preserve blood shelf life is also a way that would make it unpalatable to vampires too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-28-2022, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T14:13:49-08:00","id":1473499,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> <br /> \u200bI wonder how easy to just walk out with the stuff. Hospitals are always staffed, but if you think it's fine to one stop shop backgrounds. I think having resources 5 generated by a hospital is different than buying a hospital and giving myself carefree domain, herd, and retainers who never question my actions because I own the place and write payroll is just not right. Does the resource 5 character also have 5 in contacts and allies because money? I also agree I don't consider 5 resources a billionaire. Millions can run out, hospitals can be money sinks, people can take the money and still not follow through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T14:17:13-08:00","id":1473501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473497#post1473497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember when Resources 5 = 5 million dollars.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like older editions were better with money merits. Corporate CEO was a background I remember, Mansion was another. I'd have to pull up the old first edition pdf, but I remember there being a bunch of things like this to make resources five be more oomf.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T14:51:18-08:00","id":1473502,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Extremely Wealthy. You are the model to which others strive to achieve, at least in the popular mind. Television shows, magazine spreads, and gossip websites speculate about your clothing, the appointments of your numerous homes, and the luxury of your modes of transportation. You have vast and widely distributed assets, perhaps tied to the fates of nations, each with huge staffs and connections to every level of society through a region. You travel with a minimum of three-dot comforts, more with a little effort. Corporations and governments sometimes come to you to buy into stocks or bond programs.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think one problem with this is it's a little on the purple prose side of things and it could have done with some more explicit $ estimates. This describes the likes of Tom Cruise, Talor Swift, or Roger Federer on the upper end to me, so maybe half a billion. I can see it being ruled Billionaire by others though.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T16:07:56-08:00","id":1473506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473496#post1473496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IRL a LOT of blood that goes to a blood bank is wasted due to blood not having a great shelf life and supply/demand being inconsistent. It really probably isn't so hard for a few dozen bags to be written off each month, depending on the size of the bank.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, and due to a lot of other reasons blood embezzlement is actually a real thing. There are even some people with any of the many conditions that can lead to hematophagy that manage to legally buy blood for consumption with some regularity.<br /> <br /> What would be problems are:<br /> <br /> A) Volume. A human hematophagus consumes a bag of blood a month at most, but a vampire is consuming <i>at least</i> one or two per day (depending on which of two conflicting information in the books you use), probably more to be safe, that's a lot for most banks, and not a small scheme in any case;<br /> <br /> B) It's still not something you can assume you can do just because you own the place. Easy or hard, dangerous or safe, setting up the embezzlement scheme shouldn't be taken for granted if it isn't covered somewhere else, especially in a tightly regulated industry. While there is corruption and all that, the point isn't if it is hard, it never was;<br /> <br /> C) Game concerns. At the end of the day, what's at the center of this is how the matter affects the game, and <i>Resources</i> is still just a BG. It must be balanced against the other BGs. Not for realism, not for mathematical balance, but simply because the players must feel their choices are valid and fair, not system traps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473501#post1473501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like older editions were better with money merits. Corporate CEO was a background I remember, Mansion was another. I'd have to pull up the old first edition pdf, but I remember there being a bunch of things like this to make resources five be more oomf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Older editions gave a hard ceiling of how much you earn and how much you can get by liquidating your assets at each level of <i>Resources</i>, the problem is that this hard number does not translate well everywhere and much less age well. It was a bad idea from the beginning.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> said, this is covered in other books. To be precise, the best descriptions of several levels of <i>Resources</i> I've seen to date are in M20 (better than the Guide to Technocracy that introduced the idea of 6+ BG). Those guidelines are really good to have a better grasp about what you have at each point, although they need some time reading and digesting (they're good, but could have been better written).<br /> <br /> It runs more or less like that: up to 5 <i>Resources</i> dictates primarily personal life, how much buying power you have to establish lifestyle and acquire things or amenities. So at 5 there's no <i>personal possession</i> you can't afford, be it a vehicle, housing, whatever.<br /> <br /> At 6+ it starts to dictate <i>how much you impact local economy</i>. That's the level where you own key businesses and has enough money for your fortune to directly affect other people in a meaningful scale. A hospital probably wouldn't even be <i>Resources</i> 5 under M20 rules, although a small hospital you have little personal intervention on aside earning profit could be.<br /> <br /> Under those rules, if you have enough money to threat half a hundred people with unemployment and then follow through without any impact on your <i>Resources</i> level because that's just that small a part of your operations, then by all means you have more than 5. And even then, mind you, those rules still don't let you just use your assets to freely emulate other BGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T08:45:54-08:00","id":1473526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473484#post1473484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the first, you are right. That was not an adequate opening, I let my frustration (with many things) speak for me at the time and I shouldn't. I'm sorry about that, but I didn't edit out either as it was your right to answer it. I'll edit it out or let it in place as you wish in this particular matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I accept the apology; civility is a perishable skill and as such requires constant practice. Though if I am being honest I called it out mostly because I was curious to see if CTPhipps would practice what he preached during our last dust up. In 25+ years of using the forum that was the only time I ever got a ban, so you can understand my curiosity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473484#post1473484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the second part, I made my actual arguments from the third paragraph onward, so you basically ignored everything I actually said. Since you were possibly and rightfully angry at me still, I won't hold that against you if you want to reread the rest of the post to make an actual answer to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I avoided responding to the rest of your points until I could think about them. But even after doing so, they really all boil down to the same concept, essentially Backgrounds can't do too much because there has to be story hooks or because game logic. I tend to dismiss this line of thinking because figuring out those weaknesses or plot points are the job of the ST. I will freely admit that if the ST doesn't have real life knowledge of the subject matter then they are a lot less likely to be able to counter it. But that shouldn't be an automatic strike against the base mechanic.<br /> <br /> Resources just represents your ability to have money and income. A way to abstractly explain how you pay for things without the hassle of doing the D&amp;D thing of tracking each copper piece, silver piece, gold piece, and if I am showing my age your Electrum or Platinum pieces as well. But the key thing is that money still acts like money, Resources just covers a form of access to it.<br /> <br /> When trying to convince an NPC to do something, you can Role Play it out using your own logic and statements to the ST, the ST could just have you roll a persuasion check, you could use Dominate or Presence, or lastly you could just put a stack of cash so large in front of the NPC that their greed compels them. All of those are valid in my book.<br /> <br /> My stand point is Money can do x,y, and z. Resources give you access to a given level of money. Thus Resources if used correctly can thus allow you to do x,y, and z. <br /> <br /> I have never stated that Resources is invulnerable or auto-win in function. Yes if you own a hospital any kindred can try to break in to get blood, dominate/presence some one with access for blood packs, or they could try to do a hostile take over or bury the hospital in lawsuits so that you abandon it. But at the same time you have just as many storyline options for owning a hospital that are beneficial. Such as other vampires trading boons for access or being able to use the medical facilities for their mortal followers without a paper trail.<br /> <br /> It's funny because maintaining money i.e., Resources is harder than the game makes it out to be. A family friend thought it would be a good idea back in the 1980s to transfer money from an American bank to a Mexican bank because he was going to do some business south of the boarder. It was a great plan until the Peso value dropped considerably compared to the Dollar. As such tens of thousands of dollars devalued down to a few hundred practically overnight. So while you can gain security from investigation by hiding your Resources in different areas than where your Story is taking place, nothing says those other places can't affect your Resources score on their own. Though this also means that causing widespread financial crashes could possibly be an ear mark of inter-kindred combat.<br /> <br /> The sad thing is this debate is a lot like the old debates from Mage: the Ascension about how it didn't take much in the way of xp to get the right spheres of magic to be able to conjure nuclear weapons. The fun of an RPG is to be able to experiment with being able to do things you can't in real life. The problem is that not everyone thinks on the same scale. Tell one player that their character can conjure things and they will do little tricks to augment role play, tell another player the same thing and they will crush nations and redraw the map. I am the sort of ST that is fine with both approaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T08:55:55-08:00","id":1473527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473502#post1473502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Extremely Wealthy. You are the model to which others strive to achieve, at least in the popular mind. Television shows, magazine spreads, and gossip websites speculate about your clothing, the appointments of your numerous homes, and the luxury of your modes of transportation. You have vast and widely distributed assets, perhaps tied to the fates of nations, each with huge staffs and connections to every level of society through a region. You travel with a minimum of three-dot comforts, more with a little effort. Corporations and governments sometimes come to you to buy into stocks or bond programs.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think one problem with this is it's a little on the purple prose side of things and it could have done with some more explicit $ estimates. This describes the likes of Tom Cruise, Talor Swift, or Roger Federer on the upper end to me, so maybe half a billion. I can see it being ruled Billionaire by others though.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>They tried quantifying Backgrounds in previous editions and the problem is that it doesn't age well. The price of a nice house in a good neighborhood in the 1950s was about $35K, that same house in the 1980s would be about $110K, flash forward to today it is worth about $980K. So your time period changes all the values.<br /> <br /> Then again back in mage they said if you rolled max successes, you could summon a Pentium III laptop with a CD drive. So perhaps certain mechanics need a bit more polish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T09:27:22-08:00","id":1473530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473526#post1473526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sad thing is this debate is a lot like the old debates from Mage: the Ascension about how it didn't take much in the way of xp to get the right spheres of magic to be able to conjure nuclear weapons. The fun of an RPG is to be able to experiment with being able to do things you can't in real life. The problem is that not everyone thinks on the same scale. Tell one player that their character can conjure things and they will do little tricks to augment role play, tell another player the same thing and they will crush nations and redraw the map. I am the sort of ST that is fine with both approaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is why despite liking high powered stories I have all but given up trying to run powerful elder games. The disparity between characters with a pile of experience is really something to see. I had one friend who really didn't care if everyone else was more powerful, just wanted to roleplay a certain way, a couple more who just didn't grasp the game as well who were very frustrated by and a couple rules munchkins trying to be all powerful.<br /> <br /> I think starting out a bit more powerful (So not boring like playing a level one mage in AD&amp;D) and then growing over time turns out much greater balance as players see how things work and even laid back types want to keep up a bit to stay relevant in play and hopefully power players see the need for more rounded characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T10:21:58-08:00","id":1473535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473526#post1473526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My stand point is Money can do x,y, and z. Resources give you access to a given level of money. Thus Resources if used correctly can thus allow you to do x,y, and z.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the idea and agree, but the point is more how you make it work.<br /> <br /> By having <i>Resources</i> you have the means to achieve many things. But having the means and achieving them are the distinct things at the heart of the discussion (of this particular tangent, anyway). By no means I, as an ST, would deny a player the ability to try using their <i>Resources</i> to achieve any of those and many other goals. And the very idea of using it to own a hospital, even without the other backgrounds, isn't a bad idea.<br /> <br /> This player would have to accept the workload and risks, though, and there's where the other BGs actually matter. They directly signify a benefit, so they make things easier. You don't need to devise a scheme (for example) because the BG directly represents this and the specific benefits. You also shouldn't worry about it being of hard maintenance, again because it is already a trait in your sheet. Most of the argument here was around that: not that you can't <i>achieve</i> similar results with <i>Resources</i> alone, but that you shouldn't take it for granted in the same way.<br /> <br /> On the matter of discussing game logic, my particular problem comes from experience with groups which very distinct understanding and expectations from the game, both as player and ST, and how using just plain logic (money can do, hence it does) may result in a lot of frustration for some players in the same group that perceive this inequality. This isn't an ever present problem, but is a problem, and as an ST/designer I prefer to start from a safe place in this regard. It is easier to start from this then adapt to suit the actual group's style than start from a less forgiving place then have to remedy the harm done (I've been in both places already).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T11:00:46-08:00","id":1473537,"title":"","content":"To make a very vampiric example:<br /> <br /> &quot;A man with Resources 5 should have no ability making a body disappear with proper application of said resources. However, that doesn't mean having resources 5 gives you automatic ability to make a body disappear.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T16:59:42-08:00","id":1473546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473537#post1473537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make a very vampiric example:<br /> <br /> &quot;A man with Resources 5 should have no ability making a body disappear with proper application of said resources. However, that doesn't mean having resources 5 gives you automatic ability to make a body disappear.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2-eMOCMDQj8\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Modern Rogue: How Not to Dissolve a Body with Lye&quot;</a><br /> <br /> Lye, water, stainless steel tub, propane burner &amp; fuel. More like Resources 2 for the base components. But yes you should have to spend money to buy things which in turn allow to do other things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T17:26:10-08:00","id":1473549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470529-how-do-vampires-maintain-security-while-hunting?p=1473546#post1473546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lye, water, stainless steel tub, propane burner &amp; fuel. More like Resources 2 for the base components. But yes you should have to spend money to buy things which in turn allow to do other things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Never doubt people's ability to just not buy the right things for the project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}